  "body": "## Problem and change\n\nFix #4436 (P1, effort:high). A `table_rh` rotary needs the opposite sign from the tool-relative pose. Fanuc and Doosan DNM wrote `A30.` where the machine needed `A-30.`. The travel check also used the wrong sign on an asymmetric range.\n\nBoth G43.4 posts now apply the resolved convention when they write rotary words. The existing resolver uses the axis setting, then the machine setting, then `tool_rh`. The machine pose check uses the same signed angle. Its lone-X path applies the axis direction before the convention.\n\nThe default `tool_rh` program stays byte-identical. Modal angle memory, feed calculations, Mach4 and the chain solver do not change. No dependency, file format or process file changes.\n\nBaseline: `e80c70942c9484e22d4dfa2110590473a5e49875`.\nValidated head: `3c0dc8eb7406aaaea4ccb752c8989c3e7c94284d`.\n\n## Regression tests\n\nThe baseline fails on A30 versus A-30, asymmetric pose travel and the lone-X convention. The `tool_rh` control passes. All six pins pass in the existing `camcraft-post` `script_rotary` suite:\n\n- `rotary_sign::g43_4_posts_use_machine_and_axis_sign_conventions`\n- `rotary_sign::g43_4_tool_rh_keeps_the_default_program`\n- `rotary_sign::g43_4_travel_check_judges_the_posted_sign`\n- `rotary_sign::lone_x_travel_applies_convention_after_the_axis_direction`\n- `rotary_sign::tormach_refuses_its_own_word_outside_the_signed_travel`\n- `rotary_sign::g43_4_posts_refuse_explicit_c_live_tool_work`\n\nThe pins cover both posts, inherited and per-axis settings, initial and modal words, and acceptance and refusal at signed travel limits.\n\n## Verification\n\nAn independent agent ran these checks on the validated head, with Windows, Rust 1.100.1 and MSVC:\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Focused quick selection | PASS: all 97 executable steps; 1,978 tests passed, 6 expected ignored, zero failures. |\n| `script_rotary` | PASS: 72 tests, including all six pins. |\n| Post clippy, all targets, warnings denied | PASS. |\n| Light lane | PASS: all five executable steps and all 11 twins; zero failures or ignored tests. |\n| P1 heavy step, `app heavy: lathe_workholding_kinds` | PASS: `every_slow_kind_on_a_mill_turn_keeps_the_work_spindle_within_the_chuck` ran; one passed, zero failed or ignored, 45.73 seconds. |\n| Formatting and whitespace | New test and suite registration PASS; diff check PASS. The judge retains 12 formatter hunks, 76 edit lines, identical to the baseline. No formatting defect was introduced. |\n\n```sh\ncargo xtask gate quick --base e80c70942c9484e22d4dfa2110590473a5e49875 --only 'post suites:' --only 'app suites:'\ncargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets --locked --offline -j 4 -- -D warnings\ncargo xtask gate light --only 'motion light:' --only 'app light:'\ncargo xtask gate heavy --base e80c70942c9484e22d4dfa2110590473a5e49875 --only 'app heavy: lathe_workholding_kinds'\n```\n\nProcess environment: `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=4`, `CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off`, `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true`. No `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` override.\n\nThe quick selection runs all mapped test steps from the 99-step plan, without two redundant all-target prebuilds. The light selection runs all five test steps from the six-step plan, without its redundant prebuild. Each selected step compiles its own target. The single P1 heavy test posts Rotary Contour within the chuck and refuses unsupported five-axis kinds by name.\n\nThese existing app blocking regressions also pass on the final head:\n\n- `control_comp::the_lathe_and_the_other_mill_posts_refuse_a_control_op_by_name_and_the_gate_blocks`\n- `per_op_files::a_refusal_in_op_two_writes_nothing`\n- `c_axis_live::every_post_without_c_or_without_the_machines_words_refuses_by_name`\n\nEvidence is preserved locally in `source/.claude/tmp/4436-evidence/`: `final-head-quick.log`, `final-head-clippy.log`, `final-head-light.log`, `final-head-heavy.log`, and `verification-summary.md`. These logs are not source changes.\n\n## Scope and review\n\nThe Tormach pin checks its existing named refusal before an out-of-travel A20 word. Actual `Move::rotary` C input states `LiveTool = radial`; both G43.4 posts return the named capability warning. The app blocks any counted warning before it returns `Posted`. The engine and standalone post CLI can retain program text with warnings. This unchanged lower-level contract adds no C live-tool support or shared C-check conversion.\n\nPR #4371 was inspected at `ce23fdaa8d18ae3784604f2ad1198316cdf7277d`. Its retract and section-preamble edits do not touch the angle writer or machine judge changed here. No retract work is included. The #4417 branch was inspected at `2ede3d05710529d59bb1e0e88761977de23ea057`; its joint-angle conversion precedes this sign conversion. This PR adds no chain solver.\n\n[Decision record](https://github.com/seelesturm/Camcraft-NeoTech/blob/3c0dc8eb7406aaaea4ccb752c8989c3e7c94284d/docs/decisions/4436-rotary-sign-convention.md).\n[Writer record](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/4436#issuecomment-7229039456).\n\nNo physical control or machine run was performed. This contributor PR needs the upstream collaborator review required by the repository.\n\nEffort: high\nChangelog: Fanuc and Doosan DNM posts honor rotary sign conventions, and machine travel checks use the same signed pose angles.\n\nFixes #4436",
